ROOT: black queen on b6, attacked by white knight a4: True
move     queen capturable after? recapture takes back       net for White
e6e5     YES (a4b6)             a7b6 (net +6)              +6
b6b4     YES (d2b4)             e7b4 (net +0)              +0

So BOTH moves leave the queen capturable. The difference is what Black's recapture takes:
  e6e5  -> White Nxb6 wins QUEEN(9); black axb6 takes a KNIGHT(3)  => White +6
  b6b4  -> White Qxb4 wins QUEEN(9); black Bxb4 takes the QUEEN(9) => White +0, a TRADE
The cost is the RECAPTURE BALANCE, not whether the queen can be taken.
